course: dictionary
lesson: 9492
title: Steely: grey like metal, hard like a strong will
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Steely means made of steel, or grey and shiny like steel. «It is cold and still under a hard steely sky.» The clues are cold, still and hard, so the sky must look like grey metal.
explain: Steely can also describe a person. A «steely stare» or a «steely voice» is hard and cold, and it does not show soft feelings. «Steely determination» means someone is very strong in their wish to keep going. What word would fit here? Try hard or strong in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Steely is an adjective, so it can change: steelier and steeliest. The sky can look steelier at dusk than it did at noon, and that tells you it is getting greyer and harder to see through.
fact: «Steely» means made of steel, or grey and shiny like steel.
fact: «Steely» can describe a stare or a voice that is hard, cold and not soft.
fact: «Steely determination» means a very strong wish to keep going and not give up.
fact: Steely is an adjective, and it can change: steelier, steeliest.
fact: Hard and strong may fit in some places, but steely adds the idea of cold, grey metal.
exercise: «It is cold and still under a hard steely sky.» What does steely most likely describe here? | Loud and noisy | Sweet-smelling | Warm and soft, like a blanket | *Grey and shiny, like metal
exercise: The teacher gave Maya a steely stare. What does steely suggest? | Sleepy and tired | Happy and giggly | Wet and muddy | *Hard, cold and strong, not soft
exercise: Sam showed steely determination to finish the race. What does this mean? | He was sad and gave up | He was hungry | He was lost in the rain | *He was very determined and would not give up
test: «Her steely voice made the class go quiet.» What does steely show about her voice? | Soft and sleepy | Loud and funny | *Hard and strong, not showing soft feelings | Sweet and kind
test: In «a steely grey sea», what does steely tell you about the sea's colour? | *Grey and shiny, like steel | Muddy brown | Warm pink | Golden yellow
exam: Which sentence uses steely to mean hard and determined? | The puppy was soft and warm. | The sky was a steely grey. | *She set her jaw with steely determination. | We ate steely biscuits for tea.
